                %li
                  %a{:href => "#examples_and_models"} Examples and Models
          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In the presence of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
            in fact has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomaly"} quantum anomaly
            reflected on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tadpole"} tadpole
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagrams"} Feynman diagrams
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+perturbation+series"} string perturbation series
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-fields"} RR-fields
          %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/TadpoleCancellationFactorization.jpg", :width => "600px"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#BlumenhagenLustTheisen13"} Blumenhagen-Lüst-Theisen 13
          %p
            and reflected in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target spacetime
            by non-trivial total
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact spaces
          %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/RRTadpoleCancellation.jpg", :width => "600px"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#IbanezUranga12"} Ibanez-Uranga 12
          %p
            This anomaly cancels if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            are accompanied by a suitable collection of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O-planes"} O-planes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            backgrounds (
            %a{:href => "#Sagnotti88"}> Sagnotti 88, pp. 5
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#GimonPolchinski96"} Gimon-Polchinski 96, section 3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O-planes"} O-planes
            this means to consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+I+string+theory"} type I string theory
            instead.)
          %p
            Accordingly, tadpole cancellation via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifolds"} orientifolding
            is a key consistency condition in the construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
          %p
            Traditionally RR-tadpole cancellation is discussed in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
            should be in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
          %p
            Discussion of tadpole cancellation with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
            regarded in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            was initated in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Uranga00"} Uranga 00, Section 5
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GarciaUranga05"} Garcia-Uranga 05
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Marchesano03"} Marchesano 03, Section 4
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MarchesanoShiu04"} Marchesano-Shiu 04
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#CKMNW05"} CKMNW 05, Section 2.2
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MaidenShiuStefanski06"} Maiden-Shiu-Stefanski 06, Section 5
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#DFM09"} DFM 09, p. 6-7
          %p
            But the situation remains somewhat inconclusive (see also
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Moore14"} Moore 14, p. 21-22
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#ForFractionalDBranes In plane and toroidal orientifolds
          %p
            More details are understood in the special case of plane orbifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mi cpt
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^{cpt} \!\sslash\! G
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toroidal+orbifold"} toroidal orientifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕋
                    %mi V
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mo ⫽
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^V \!\sslash\! G
            where
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+D-branes"} fractional D-branes
            may be stuck at
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            singularities, whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
            is supposed to be in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
            of the point, hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} representation ring
            of the given
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotropy+group"} isotropy group
          %h3#InTermsOfEquivariantKTheory In terms of equivariant K-theory / the representation ring
          %p
            In this case tadpole cancellation conditions are given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theoretic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations"} equations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/character+of+a+linear+representation"} characters
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+representations"} linear representations
            corresponding to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+D-branes"} fractional D-branes
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [1]
                  \\subset
                  [H_1]
                  \\subset
                  [H_2]
                  \\subset
                  \\cdots
                  \\subset
                  [G]
          %p
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+extension+of+a+partial+order"} linear extension
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partially+ordered+set"} partially ordered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+of+subgroups"} lattice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} sub-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+order"} linear order
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ⟩
                    %mo ]
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ⟩
                    %mo ]
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
