              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/EquCohomotopyImpliesGlobalTadCancellation.jpg", :width => "800"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiber19"} Sati-Schreiber 19
          %h3#ExamplesForFractionalDBranes Examples of non-compact singularities
          %p
            We discuss more explicitly the solutions to the local/twisted tadpole cancellation condition
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:VanishingOfCharacterValuesOnNontrivialSubgroups"} (2)
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+D-branes"} fractional D-branes
            at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singularities"} singularities
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isotropy+group"} isotropy group
            one of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+group"} non-abelian
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroups+of+SU%282%29"} finite subgroups of SU(2)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi DE
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G_{DE}
                  \\;\subset\;
                  SU(2)
          %p
            hence those in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-classification"} D- and E-series
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+dihedral+groups"} binary dihedral groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 D_{2n}
            and the three exceptional cases:
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2T"} 2T
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2O"} 2O
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2I"} 2I
          %p
            For these groups, by
            %a{:href => "#BurtonSatiSchreiber18"} BSS 18, Theorem 4.1
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+representation"} virtual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representations"} permutation representations
            span precisely the sub charge lattice of integral (non-irrational) characters/RR-charges in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            charge lattice of the corresponding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularity"} ADE-singularity
            = succeed "=" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+KO-theory"} equivariant KO-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} real representation ring
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi KO
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mi DE
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi RO
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi DE
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  KO^0_{G_{DE}}(\ast)
                  \\;=\;
                  RO\left( G_{DE} \right)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Since the tadpole cancellation condition
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:VanishingOfCharacterValuesOnNontrivialSubgroups"} (2)
            in particular requires the characters/charges to be integral (specifically: zero) the general solution to the tadpole cancellation condition is indeed in this sub-lattice, and so that is where we may and do solve it, below.
          %p
            In accord with the general Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RegularRepSpansSolutionToHomogeneousTadpoleCancellation"}
            we find that in each case there is precisely a 1-dimensional (i.e.
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} representation ring
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:VanishingOfCharacterValuesOnNontrivialSubgroups"} (2)
            = succeed "-multiples" do
